    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.IsOrthonormalL2: L:phase-bessel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:72-74 requires '∀ k j, MemLp (u k j) 2 μ' and '∫ η, ∑ j, u k j η * conj (u l j η) ∂μ = if k = l then 1 else 0'; TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:347-348 requires a 'finite orthonormal family in L^2(R^d;C^2)'. Componentwise L² membership and this integral identity encode precisely that hypothesis after specialization. The first-slot-linear convention is supported by TeX:169-176. Ledger:2408 and lean/claims.yaml:6773-6779 faithfully summarize it."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.coeff: E:phase-bessel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:78-79 defines '∫ η, ∑ j, u k j η • g j η ∂μ', without integrability hypotheses on the definition. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:348-351 assumes L² data and uses exactly '∫∑ u_{k,j}(η)g_j(η)dη'. Ledger:2409 and lean/claims.yaml:6780-6786 match; existence for the manuscript data is separately proved, not assumed by this definition."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.memLp_conj: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:83-85 states '(hf : MemLp f 2 μ) : MemLp (fun η => conj (f η)) 2 μ'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:348-359 assumes L² orthonormal data and invokes the conjugated family, but does not separately state this arbitrary-measure lemma. Ledger:2410 correctly calls it a Lean-route auxiliary; lean/claims.yaml:6787-6793 matches its type."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.integrable_mul_of_memLp: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:89-91 assumes 'MemLp f 2 μ' and 'MemLp h 2 μ' and concludes 'Integrable (fun η => f η * h η) μ'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:348-349 assumes L² data and :363 invokes 'L² Cauchy–Schwarz', without separately stating this scalar-product lemma. Ledger:2411 and lean/claims.yaml:6794-6800 are faithful; no direct label is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.integrable_smul_of_memLp: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:93-99 assumes '(hf : MemLp f 2 μ) (hh : MemLp h 2 μ)' and concludes integrability of 'f η • h η', explicitly omitting completeness. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:347-349 uses Hilbert-valued L² data and :363 says 'The Bochner integrals exist by L² Cauchy–Schwarz'. This more general helper is accurately described as a Lean-route auxiliary in ledger:2412 and lean/claims.yaml:6801-6807."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.integrable_coeff_integrand: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:101-107 assumes '∀ k j, MemLp (u k j) 2 μ' and '∀ j, MemLp (g j) 2 μ', with finite J but no finite-family or completeness requirement, and proves coefficient-integrand integrability. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:348-349 has orthonormal L² data and :363 asserts that the Bochner integrals exist. Ledger:2413 and lean/claims.yaml:6808-6814 correctly describe the weaker-hypothesis helper rather than claiming it is a separate labelled manuscript result."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.integrable_sum_norm_sq: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:109-114 assumes '∀ j, MemLp (g j) 2 μ' and concludes 'Integrable (fun η => ∑ j, ‖g j η‖ ^ 2) μ', without an inner-product or completeness assumption. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:349 assumes 'g ∈ L²(R^d;H²)' and :352 uses the corresponding squared-norm integral. Ledger:2414 and lean/claims.yaml:6815-6821 faithfully state this unlabelled integrability auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.residual_expand: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:116-125 takes arbitrary finite arrays 'a', 'y', 'x', without orthonormality or completeness, and proves the residual identity with '- 2 * re' and the stated double sum. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:360-362 describes 'subtracting an orthogonal finite projection and expanding its nonnegative squared norm', but does not state this Hilbert-valued array identity. Ledger:2415 explicitly identifies Mathlib's conjugate-linear-first inner product, and lean/claims.yaml:6822-6828 matches the formula. The different proof route is disclosed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.phase_bessel: L:phase-bessel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:65-67,169-173 assumes a complete complex inner-product space, finite indices, '(hu : IsOrthonormalL2 μ u)' and '(hg : ∀ j, MemLp (g j) 2 μ)'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:347-349 assumes a separable complex Hilbert space, a finite orthonormal L²(R^d;C²) family and g in L²(R^d;H²). Lean proves the identical inequality with constant 1, plus integrability, under explicitly disclosed generalizations. Ledger:2416 and lean/claims.yaml:6829-6835 match. Neither σ-finiteness nor a supplied analytic input is required."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.isOrthonormalL2_conj: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:222-233 assumes 'hu : IsOrthonormalL2 μ u' and concludes orthonormality of 'fun k j η => conj (u k j η)', without requiring finite ι. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:348 assumes an orthonormal family, and :359 uses 'the orthonormal family {overline(u_k)}'. Ledger:2417 and lean/claims.yaml:6836-6842 faithfully describe the general helper; 'no direct label' avoids assigning it a separate manuscript result."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.phase_bessel_conj: L:phase-bessel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/PhaseBessel.lean:240-246 assumes '(hu : IsOrthonormalL2 μ u) (hg : ∀ j, MemLp (g j) 2 μ)' and proves the conjugated coefficient bound and integrability. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:347-349 supplies the corresponding specialized hypotheses and :354 states 'The same bound holds with overline(u_{k,j}) in place of u_{k,j}'. Conjugation, constant 1 and inequality direction agree. Ledger:2418 and lean/claims.yaml:6843-6849 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.PhaseBessel.phase_bessel_paper: L:phase-bessel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
