      "reason": "candidate/statement-ledger.md:2364-2404 accurately identifies the manuscript statement and proof ranges, componentwise L² encoding, inner-product convention, arbitrary-measure and finite-component generality, unused separability, absence of supplied analytic inputs, and different projection proof. Removing the model assumptions in manuscript/notes/integrated_wave_variance.tex:5-8 is harmless: the lemma at :346-366 concerns arbitrary Hilbert-valued L² data and uses none of the covariance parameters. Lean:169-220 proves the disclosed route. The paragraph does not claim the later variance applications."
